Description: An R port and extension of 'KernelSynth', the synthetic data
    generator used to pretrain the 'Chronos' forecasting models
    (Ansari et al., 2024, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2403.07815>). Time series are
    drawn from Gaussian process priors whose covariance is a random
    composition (sums, products, changepoints) of base kernels. On top of
    the original kernel bank, the package offers a frequency-aware extended
    bank (Matern, Brownian, polynomial, spectral mixture, locally periodic
    kernels), randomized hyperparameters, input warping, a library of
    augmentations (trends, level shifts, heteroscedasticity, outliers,
    positivity, intermittency, counts, missing values), multivariate series
    via a linear model of coregionalization, 'TSMixup', train/test task
    splits and meta-features for meta-learning. All generators return
    'ts' objects. S3 and R6 interfaces are provided.
